{
  "_doc": [
    "The UGens under test, one entry per row, keyed by U milestone.",
    "",
    "A subject is a SynthDef JSON fragment plus the little that a driver needs",
    "to know about it: what to feed it, and which of the audio-testing rules",
    "apply. Two consumers read this file and must keep agreeing:",
    "",
    "  - tests/common/bench.rs, which turns a subject into a def and runs the",
    "    generic rules over it (block split, long run, finiteness);",
    "  - examples/audition.py, the by-ear bench, which sends the same fragment",
    "    to a server so you can listen to exactly what the asserts measured.",
    "",
    "Fields. `name` is the audition handle (lowercase, unique across the file).",
    "`kind` is the registry row. `inputs` are its wire inputs in wire order.",
    "`static` carries non-signal fields (`max_delay`, ...). `source` names a",
    "signal wired in front as UGen 0, which the inputs reach as {\"ugen\": 0}:",
    "one of noise, impulse, sine, silence, dc. `hz` is the fundamental a",
    "spectral measurement should use. `traits` select the generic rules:",
    "",
    "  stateful    carries state between blocks: earns the split and long-run",
    "              drivers. A memoryless row (the pan laws) does not.",
    "  oscillator  a periodic source: earns the alias-SNR report.",
    "  stochastic  a random source: its stream must replay from its seed, so",
    "              the split driver compares it exactly rather than to a",
    "              tolerance.",
    "  finite      ends on its own (a ramp, an envelope): the long-run driver",
    "              checks where it lands rather than that it keeps going.",
    "",
    "Adding a row to a milestone is one entry here: the asserts and the ear",
    "both pick it up with no further work."
  ],

